<title>Yemen and the Red Sea: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/yemen/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-yemen-2026-11-18T14:22:43.561Z</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:22:43 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Houthis have seized the Bab al-Mandeb strait and surrounding positions after Yemeni government forces withdrew, securing the key maritime chokepoint and moving within about 60 km of Aden. Saudi Arabia dismissed its coalition commander as anti-Houthi forces pulled back from the strait and other key areas. The Yemeni parliament approved a law designating the Houthis as terrorists, raising concerns of a resurgence by southern separatists. Saudi-backed forces in Yemen have stepped up attacks on Houthi positions, while the coalition has hit dozens of Houthi military sites. The conflict caused 918 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.un.org/feed/view/en/story/2026/11/1168830&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqgFBVV95cUxPanZPTTZ6QzdLcEd4bzlITmRjVl9GOUxMaHczSGd1MkNfTDl0UnBzYWt1cl94SkNXQS0zZWZhSTZwVjBNUVd1X2JSVXpHNEJPVm1yZ0ZvZkUxM2VneHpwQ1pnc3VUT0FxQlJLR1FnLS1UOU9nOUNnYWhpUVRSdnA4TzFjUjRpLVhxai0yTkp4VlhTdGhXRWx5em50QXR4RVRvWW5MNi1OZUZQdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
</item>
